WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.280
December 1981. The US
government had more than 560

2
00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:08.700
million pounds of cheese
in its warehouses.

3
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.160
That month, the President
ordered 30 million pounds given

4
00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:14.580
away free to people in need.

5
00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:18.080
How did a government end up
with a mountain of cheese?

6
00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:21.140
It began with a promise to dairy farmers.

7
00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:24.480
Why would a government ever
make something cost more?

8
00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:28.160
In this mission, you'll draw a
price floor above equilibrium,

9
00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:30.780
and see how buyers and sellers respond.

10
00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:33.680
Then you'll raise a
guaranteed price yourself,

11
00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:35.550
and track the government's bill.

12
00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:38.580
Your mission: find out why
a government would ever

13
00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:40.050
make something cost more.
